events.body:
@murchandamus

From the old consensus changes (BIP16, BIP30, BIP34), I don't remember there was already this situation where a consensus change would significantly close some scaling technical options. I guess there has been indeed some when Satoshi did restrain the DoSy Script interpreter opcode like OP_CAT and friends), though Satoshi era style of way consensus changes were done it's not likely the standard we're adhering now...More recently with BIP141, I think it did rule out other approach of fixing malleability (e.g thing like BIP140), though was BIP140 enabling some protocols than one cannot with BIP141, I don't think at all.

To me, though correct me if you see other historical examples, I think it's a bit of a novel situation. Therefore, yeah in my view it's better to add a succinct note mentioning the impact BIP54 has on the "forward block" idea. For sure I can update with a link referencing the "forward block" paper, introduce the idea in two-sentences and link to criticism and its sum-up, all in a succinct comment, as well it's a footnote.
